From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:35:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(repository): candidate C: group commit of contact writes

S0.4 candidate C (PLAN 11.3; D17), on top of B. The four contact writes
(create, edit, cycle, delete; /contacts and /forms/submit) are queued for
a writer thread instead of taking the writer's lock on the loop. The
thread takes every write waiting, up to 100, runs them in one
BEGIN IMMEDIATE ... COMMIT, and posts each result back to the loop that
queued it, one next_tick per loop per batch. The handler answers from
that continuation, after the commit, with the row read back on the writer
inside the transaction, so what a client sees is unchanged. A write that
fails alone (a constraint, a missing row) fails alone; a lost transaction
fails the whole batch. No timer: a lone write waits only for the hop.

front logs a request only when its handler returned answered; the
continuations log their own line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
